  "_meta": {
    "file": "phantom-normal.json",
    "version": "0.4.0-draft",
    "status": "DRAFT — geometry is schematic; validate with an echo-lab fellow/cardiologist (planned after P2/P3). Tune visually with the dev calibration mode described in views.json._calibration.",
    "units": "cm, degrees, time as fraction of RR interval (t=0 at R-wave peak = end-diastole)",
    "references": [
      "Lang RM et al. Recommendations for cardiac chamber quantification. JASE 2015;28:1-39",
      "Mitchell C et al. ASE Guidelines for performing a comprehensive TTE examination in adults. JASE 2019;32:1-64",
      "POCUS101 Cardiac Ultrasound Made Easy (primary teaching reference)",
      "Netter, Atlas of Human Anatomy, plates 215–229 (private reference: relations only, no images or text in the app)",
      "Ramathibodi RAID204 lectures: Heart and great vessels; Lung and mediastinum; Thoracic wall (what learners must identify)",
      "Non-contrast gated cardiac CT, Kaggle archive (1): base-of-heart position/size only (descending aorta ≈2.4 cm, ≈0.5 cm behind the LA; sternum→spine ≈10 cm at the base)"
    ],
    "supersedes": "Plan v1.1 §1.1/§1.2: LV long-axis orientation refined (≈50° left of sagittal, ≈35° inferior, ≈17° anterior) so that PLAX is reachable with a near-perpendicular beam; LV ES length 7.2 cm with MAPSE 1.3 cm (was 7.5).",
    "changelog": [
      "0.2.0: heart moved 1.2 cm posterior (RV free wall was touching the chest wall; RV now ~2 cm deep in PLAX); descending aorta moved to stay just behind the LA; rib width 1.3→1.0 cm and AP thickness 1.0→0.8 cm (realistic intercostal windows); liver left lobe enlarged (subxiphoid window); lung cardiac notch enlarged (apical window opens in LLD). All found by rendering the views and tracing the centre scan line.",
      "0.3.0: anatomy realism pass after staff-style review of renders — curved/tapered MV+TV leaflets with free-edge curl, AV cusp belly sag, bullet-shaped LV, organic atria (vestibules, PV ostia, LAA, SVC, RA appendage, carved IAS, LA–aorta wall), thicker pericardium; echo: myocardium/liver mottling. Pericardium thinner except posteriorly; leaflet width-arc (short-axis curvature). LA moved posterior (under the aortic root, as in PLAX); mitral annulus tilted; descending aorta moved posterior-left to stay behind the LA.",
      "0.4.0 (P1.5, in progress): 3D heart meshed from the signed distance of the heart's outer surface (gHeartD) at 0.13 cm, bake skips the body wall (the anterior RV had been cut flat by the chest-wall layer). Base of the heart re-laid round the aortic root (clock face from above): LA moved behind the root at sinus level (no false-ASD look in PLAX), PV anterior-left of the AV, RVOT/conus a curved tube from the TV side over the front of the aorta to the PV (PSAX-AV: RV/RVOT wraps the Mercedes sign), LAA a tapering finger beside the PA trunk, LVOT a tube along the aortic axis with the basal IVS continuing into the anterior aortic wall and the AML hinged on the posterior aortic annulus. New label ids LA_wall, RA_wall (IAS now only where both atria meet). Views: PLAX beam ⟂ the LV–aorta bisector; plane3 lateral now lies in the derived plane (side landmark only picks the sign); A4C notch side = LV_lateral_mid."
    ]
  },
